    Back in 2023, I started two fanfics from the Beauty and the Beasts Webcomic and Webnovel.
    I wanted to think about how things would be different for Bai Qingqing and Curtis's snake babies. With Curtis's memories of being loved and cared for by his spouse, it could give the next generation more hope.
    One of our MCs, Bo, was born in chapter 1182 of the novel to Bai Qingqing and Curtis.


Chapter 1: Chapter 1: The Beginning
Chapter Text

Anna stared at her phone for a second.

She would have loved to have texted someone something like "I'm headed out for a hike. If I don't text in a day or two, send help." Something funny like that to her best friend.

But, her phone had some co-workers and some acquaintances. No family anymore. No bestie.

 

She sighed and finished shoving some protein bars in her backpack.

She was going to enjoy her day off damn it.

 

It was finally nice enough to get back out into the woods.

She hopped in her little car and headed out to a spot. Not her favorite but a hike close by. The summer heat oozed out of the car and made it smell dusty.

The ride up was nice. The sky was a promising blue with gentle fluffy clouds. It seemed like it was going to be a day of good weather.

Only two other cars were parked at the trail head.

Anna smiled to herself.

"I might be lonely, but at least I won't have to awkwardly edge past anyone else." She said to the empty passenger seat. Sighing.

Today was going to be a good day. She had decided it would be, so she was making it a good day.

The car door shut. Anna pulled her bag up over her shoulder and she headed up the dirt path.

The green everywhere smelled amazing!

Up and up she went, enjoying the light trickling in over the trees.

 

A misstep. The ground seemed to sink. Maybe a rock slipped? Gravity felt weird.

"What the fuck?" she spat. The corners of her vision went fuzzy, like tv static.

(It's alright.) She thought to herself, reaching behind her to touch her bag. (We just need to hydrate.)

Pain shot through her head. The fuzzy vision blurred into blackness and purple spiderwebs.

She fell to her knees, clutching her head in her hands when she felt like she was falling. She clutched at anything, finding nothing there.

Unable to see, unable to feel the ground, she flailed and started screaming!
