The next morning she turned on her side by herself! She put her hand on his cool tail and sighed.

(Did someone take me to a hospital?) She wondered. She could feel the bandages around her chest.
She opened her eyes. A muscular man with long black hair melted into a big red snake that coiled around her.

“Well hello there beautiful figment of my imagination.” She beamed up at him. “Look at you. Aren’t you just perfect.”
She reached up and coiled his hair around her finger.
“I love your hair.”

He handed her a warm mug of something pungent.
“Oh thank you!” She sipped. “God, I’m sorry. I guess I’m not feeling up for this right now. I’ll try again later.”

 

~~~

Her eyes fluttered and slowly opened.
“Ha!” She stated, gazing up at him with glassy eyes. She seemed to look him over, her eyes trailing down his torso and onto his long tail.

“Look!” She said. Her hand sprang up to float and flapped for a bit.

“Give her more blade leaf tea while the rice cooks.” The doctor told Bo.

Bo handed her the mug.
“Oh, I’ll puke. Don’t have the energy to puke.”

She took a sip anyway. Her eyebrows sprang together. She shook her head weakly.

“Hungry.” She groaned.

“GET HER SOME FO-OD!” The crack in Bo’s voice was enough to let his desperation seep through.

The doctor was relieved. In that moment, he could feel how much devotion the snake had. Maybe his female would be alright after all.

She fell back asleep for a few minutes, curled against his tail.
Bo’s heart had been pounding in his chest since they had arrived. Every time she shifted or moaned, it seemed like it made it so much worse!

He jumped a bit when he noticed her, as she gazed up at him and smiled.
“I’m still dreaming. Sexy sci-fi snake man. Better not be sci-fi bullshit when I wake up!” Her eyes closed again. “You better be, normal guy when I wake up.”
He shifted his legs out of his snake form beside her face.

